1
00:00:04,755 --> 00:00:06,817
I thought you didn't like taking the lord's name in vain?

2
00:00:06,841 --> 00:00:08,217
Oh, shut up.

3
00:00:11,053 --> 00:00:12,138
It's been a while, huh?

4
00:00:12,346 --> 00:00:13,139
Don't blame me.

5
00:00:13,347 --> 00:00:14,891
You're the one who had a heart attack.

6
00:00:15,141 --> 00:00:18,311
Mm, the doctor did say I needed to get more exercise.

7
00:00:18,519 --> 00:00:20,396
I think he meant walks around the block.

8
00:00:20,605 --> 00:00:24,442
No, he winked at me, and did this little rotation with his hips, like...

9
00:00:27,737 --> 00:00:28,488
Mm.

10
00:00:28,696 --> 00:00:29,696
Hmm.

11
00:00:29,989 --> 00:00:31,866
Hey, we got any plans this weekend?

12
00:00:32,950 --> 00:00:37,872
I thought maybe we could get started on the vegetable garden, and then, of course, church on Sunday.

13
00:00:38,080 --> 00:00:43,836
Yeah, that does sound fun, but what if, instead, I was to go up to bethy creek with Georgie and do some fishing?

14
00:00:44,045 --> 00:00:46,297
How long you been waiting to spring that on me?

15
00:00:46,506 --> 00:00:48,549
Well, not till I was done rotating my hips.

16
00:00:48,758 --> 00:00:50,218
You're awful.

17
00:00:51,969 --> 00:00:53,054
So what do you say?

18
00:00:56,307 --> 00:00:57,308
What about Sheldon?

19
00:00:58,309 --> 00:00:59,309
What about him?

20
00:00:59,435 --> 00:01:00,435
George.

21
00:01:00,520 --> 00:01:02,063
You can't always leave him out.

22
00:01:02,271 --> 00:01:03,648
I'm not leaving him out.

23
00:01:03,856 --> 00:01:05,316
You know how he is about fishing.

24
00:01:06,108 --> 00:01:07,276
Get it away, get it away!

25
00:01:07,485 --> 00:01:08,885
Calm down, it's an itty-bitty thing.

26
00:01:09,028 --> 00:01:11,030
No, I'm an itty-bitty thing!

27
00:01:11,531 --> 00:01:13,366
Who says you have to take him fishing?

28
00:01:13,574 --> 00:01:14,934
Find something else to do with him.

29
00:01:14,992 --> 00:01:16,035
Something he'd like.

30
00:01:16,244 --> 00:01:18,871
What are we gonna do? Spend the weekend sitting around, thinking?

31
00:01:19,163 --> 00:01:19,956
George.

32
00:01:20,164 --> 00:01:21,582
You have to make an effort.

33
00:01:21,791 --> 00:01:25,336
Young boys who don't spend time with their daddies grow up to be oddballs.

34
00:01:25,545 --> 00:01:28,631
Honey, I hate to tell you, but that ball is already pretty odd.

35
00:01:30,883 --> 00:01:31,884
Please.

36
00:01:35,179 --> 00:01:36,264
Okay, fine.

37
00:01:38,266 --> 00:01:39,946
I'll talk to him. We'll think of something.

38
00:01:40,017 --> 00:01:40,685
Good.

39
00:01:40,893 --> 00:01:42,603
Thank you.

40
00:01:45,773 --> 00:01:46,773
What?

41
00:01:47,608 --> 00:01:49,777
I was just remembering when I took him camping.

42
00:01:49,986 --> 00:01:51,112
Moth! Moth!

43
00:01:51,320 --> 00:01:52,923
George sr.: Sheldon, it's just a butterfly.

44
00:01:52,947 --> 00:01:54,073
How is that any better?

45
00:01:54,282 --> 00:01:56,075
Butterfly, butterfly!

46
00:01:58,035 --> 00:02:06,210
J'j' nobody else is stronger than I am j'j' j'j' yesterday I moved a mountain j'j' n I bet I could be your hero I!”

47
00:02:06,419 --> 00:02:12,466
N I am a mighty little man n“ n I am a mighty little man. I!”

48
00:02:21,726 --> 00:02:25,187
Hey, pal playing with your rockets?

49
00:02:25,438 --> 00:02:28,149
I'm trying to calculate ballistic coefficients.

50
00:02:29,150 --> 00:02:30,776
Well, that's fun, too.

51
00:02:31,193 --> 00:02:34,980
Listen, I don't have to work this weekend; I was wondering if you wanted to do something together.

52
00:02:35,281 --> 00:02:36,281
Like what?

53
00:02:36,741 --> 00:02:37,950
Whatever you want.

54
00:02:38,534 --> 00:02:40,734
Well, the filter on my air purifier needs to be changed.

55
00:02:40,870 --> 00:02:42,121
How about a trip to sears?

56
00:02:42,663 --> 00:02:45,665
Yeah, I was thinking along the lines of something a little more active.

57
00:02:46,125 --> 00:02:48,168
Like last year, we went fishing...

58
00:02:48,252 --> 00:02:50,463
Mom! Dad's trying to make me go fishing!

59
00:02:50,671 --> 00:02:52,298
No, no, it's okay.

60
00:02:53,132 --> 00:02:54,425
We're not going fishing.

61
00:02:55,885 --> 00:02:56,927
All right, good.

62
00:02:57,136 --> 00:02:59,489
But seriously, was fishing really that bad?

63
00:02:59,513 --> 00:03:02,975
Mom! Dad's trying to convince me that fishing wasn't that bad!

64
00:03:03,184 --> 00:03:04,310
Shh. Come on!

65
00:03:04,518 --> 00:03:05,958
Forget I said anything about fishing.

66
00:03:07,021 --> 00:03:09,690
Just think about it, and we'll do whatever you want.

67
00:03:10,524 --> 00:03:11,524
Thank you.

68
00:03:14,236 --> 00:03:17,073
There is the launching of the space shuttle this weekend.

69
00:03:17,365 --> 00:03:18,574
Space shuttle?

70
00:03:19,075 --> 00:03:20,435
Don't they do those out of Florida?

71
00:03:20,534 --> 00:03:22,286
Yes. Cape canaveral.

72
00:03:23,871 --> 00:03:26,999
Sheldon, that's-that's like a12, 15 hour drive.

73
00:03:27,958 --> 00:03:30,336
I understand. Never mind.

74
00:03:32,254 --> 00:03:33,464
You know what? Let's do it.

75
00:03:34,048 --> 00:03:35,132
It'll be fun.

76
00:03:35,341 --> 00:03:37,468
The three Cooper boys on a little adventure.

77
00:03:37,885 --> 00:03:38,885
Sound good?

78
00:03:39,804 --> 00:03:40,888
Sounds good.

79
00:03:43,516 --> 00:03:45,810
My plan was coming together.

80
00:03:46,018 --> 00:03:51,524
I just needed to get on the shuttle so I could finally escape this ridiculous planet.

81
00:03:52,149 --> 00:03:55,069
Spoiler alert, I'm still here.

82
00:03:55,444 --> 00:03:59,699
So, Sheldon, me, and Georgie are gonna take a little road trip this weekend, see the shuttle launch.

83
00:04:00,032 --> 00:04:01,534
Looks like I don't get a vote in this.

84
00:04:01,742 --> 00:04:03,244
Oh, good, you're catching on.

85
00:04:03,452 --> 00:04:05,663
I wonder if we'll get to meet an astronaut.

86
00:04:05,871 --> 00:04:10,292
I remember when I was a teenager, I had the biggest crush on John Glenn.

87
00:04:10,501 --> 00:04:12,503
I would've given it up for him no problem.

88
00:04:12,795 --> 00:04:14,505
Mom. Given what up?

89
00:04:14,755 --> 00:04:16,132
Her allowance. Just eat.

90
00:04:16,340 --> 00:04:17,842
So how long are you gonna be gone?

91
00:04:18,092 --> 00:04:22,972
Oh, we'll leave first thing Saturday morning, stay the night in a motel, and see the launch bright and early on Sunday.

92
00:04:23,180 --> 00:04:26,600
I can't believe we're going to see an actual working spacecraft.

93
00:04:27,017 --> 00:04:28,352
Look how happy he is.

94
00:04:28,561 --> 00:04:29,561
Good job.

95
00:04:29,603 --> 00:04:30,771
How come I don't get to go?

96
00:04:30,980 --> 00:04:33,649
'Cause you, me, and meemaw are gonna have our own fun.

97
00:04:33,899 --> 00:04:35,693
Could we shoot guns at the gun range?

98
00:04:35,901 --> 00:04:37,903
Mm, you're too young to go to the gun range.

99
00:04:38,112 --> 00:04:39,321
Meemaw took me.

100
00:04:39,530 --> 00:04:41,240
We pinky swore. What are you doing?

101
00:04:41,741 --> 00:04:42,741
Oh, yeah.

102
00:04:42,825 --> 00:04:43,576
Don't listen to me.

103
00:04:43,784 --> 00:04:45,619
I don't know what I'm saying.

104
00:04:50,666 --> 00:04:56,172
I know you like to just keep driving, and get where you're going, but you can't ignore his bathroom schedule. I know.

105
00:04:56,380 --> 00:05:06,307
He goes number one first thing in the morning, then again in the afternoon, once more in the late afternoon, say 4:00, 4:30, depending on his juice intake, and then, a quick piddle before bedtime.

106
00:05:06,515 --> 00:05:10,120
"Piddle." got it. Now, number two's a little trickier.

107
00:05:10,144 --> 00:05:11,144
Mary? Relax.

108
00:05:11,187 --> 00:05:12,313
I can take care of my son.

109
00:05:13,314 --> 00:05:13,939
I know.

110
00:05:14,148 --> 00:05:14,815
Good.

111
00:05:15,024 --> 00:05:18,736
I'm just saying, if he's upset or nervous, he can get all clogged up.

112
00:05:18,944 --> 00:05:20,196
I won't let that happen.

113
00:05:20,696 --> 00:05:21,696
Thank you.

114
00:05:22,281 --> 00:05:23,401
Okay, let's talk about food.

115
00:05:23,532 --> 00:05:24,532
No need to.

116
00:05:25,451 --> 00:05:30,080
He likes his meat cooked to at least 165 degrees, except for chicken, which is 180.

117
00:05:30,289 --> 00:05:32,489
The different foods can't touch each other on the plate.

118
00:05:32,625 --> 00:05:34,627
Ketchup and mustard must come out of a packet.

119
00:05:34,877 --> 00:05:35,877
No bottles.

120
00:05:38,214 --> 00:05:39,840
What about his issues with spaghetti?

121
00:05:41,217 --> 00:05:41,967
That's a trick question.

122
00:05:42,176 --> 00:05:43,176
He likes spaghetti.

123
00:05:44,595 --> 00:05:46,096
All right, I guess you got this.

124
00:05:58,734 --> 00:05:59,485
Georgie.

125
00:05:59,693 --> 00:06:00,820
Up and at 'em.

126
00:06:04,406 --> 00:06:05,574
Missy, where's your brother?

127
00:06:05,825 --> 00:06:07,493
Who cares?

128
00:06:15,918 --> 00:06:16,919
Sheldon, you in there?

129
00:06:17,127 --> 00:06:17,753
Dad!

130
00:06:17,962 --> 00:06:18,963
Sorry, Georgie.

131
00:06:20,297 --> 00:06:21,465
What's going on?

132
00:06:21,715 --> 00:06:23,384
I can't find Sheldon.

133
00:06:23,968 --> 00:06:25,408
What do you mean, you can't find him?

134
00:06:25,594 --> 00:06:27,346
I mean I don't know where he is.

135
00:06:27,680 --> 00:06:29,640
Well, he's got to be somewhere.

136
00:06:30,099 --> 00:06:32,059
Maybe he got that time machine to work.

137
00:06:34,812 --> 00:06:35,479
Where the hell...

138
00:06:35,688 --> 00:06:37,064
George.

139
00:06:38,774 --> 00:06:40,609
I think he's ready to go.

140
00:06:46,031 --> 00:06:46,657
Wait, Georgie.

141
00:06:46,866 --> 00:06:48,659
Where's your bag? Don't need one.

142
00:06:48,868 --> 00:06:50,028
Got my toothbrush right here.

143
00:06:50,160 --> 00:06:51,287
What about clothes?

144
00:06:51,620 --> 00:06:52,705
A change of underwear?

145
00:06:53,581 --> 00:06:54,206
Got it.

146
00:06:54,415 --> 00:06:56,500
Georgie, you're gonna be gone for two days.

147
00:06:56,792 --> 00:06:57,918
I'll turn them inside out.

148
00:06:59,336 --> 00:07:00,504
Shotgun! No, no.

149
00:07:00,713 --> 00:07:02,393
Let your brother sit up front for a change.

150
00:07:02,548 --> 00:07:04,028
I actually prefer sitting in the back.

151
00:07:04,216 --> 00:07:04,925
It's safer.

152
00:07:05,134 --> 00:07:07,386
Oh, come on, sit up front with your daddy.

153
00:07:07,595 --> 00:07:09,355
He doesn't get to spend enough time with you.

154
00:07:09,471 --> 00:07:10,848
I called shotgun.

155
00:07:11,390 --> 00:07:12,390
George.

156
00:07:13,434 --> 00:07:14,560
We'll flip a coin.

157
00:07:14,768 --> 00:07:16,562
All right? Georgie, call it.

158
00:07:16,770 --> 00:07:17,897
Heads.

159
00:07:19,648 --> 00:07:20,316
Tails.

160
00:07:20,524 --> 00:07:21,684
Dang it. Sheldon, you won.

161
00:07:21,859 --> 00:07:23,027
You get to ride up front.

162
00:07:23,235 --> 00:07:24,486
Can't we do two out of three?

163
00:07:24,695 --> 00:07:26,739
You won. Get in the car.

164
00:07:26,947 --> 00:07:28,824
What's the point in calling shotgun?

165
00:07:29,575 --> 00:07:30,618
You're a good dad.

166
00:07:30,826 --> 00:07:33,107
If I don't kill one of them before Sunday, I'm a good dad.

167
00:07:34,371 --> 00:07:35,456
Have fun.

168
00:07:36,665 --> 00:07:38,417
Love you guys.

169
00:07:38,626 --> 00:07:40,461
Bye! Drive safe!

170
00:07:47,509 --> 00:07:52,973
Oh, this was a good idea, this was a good idea, this was a good idea.

171
00:07:56,060 --> 00:07:57,853
This was a good idea.

172
00:08:00,105 --> 00:08:01,398
Isn't this exciting?

173
00:08:01,607 --> 00:08:04,610
It's just us girls, no boys in the house.

174
00:08:04,818 --> 00:08:06,098
The place already smells better.

175
00:08:07,196 --> 00:08:08,238
So what are we gonna do?

176
00:08:08,447 --> 00:08:12,534
How would you like to go to the beauty salon and get all done up?

177
00:08:12,785 --> 00:08:14,495
Can I have orange hair like cyndi lauper?

178
00:08:15,454 --> 00:08:16,622
I don't think so.

179
00:08:16,830 --> 00:08:18,832
Meemaw has friends with blue hair.

180
00:08:19,291 --> 00:08:20,291
She's right.

181
00:08:21,043 --> 00:08:24,755
I haven't gone there yet, but after a certain age, it's mandatory.

182
00:08:25,965 --> 00:08:27,508
Your hair's not changing color.

183
00:08:27,716 --> 00:08:29,301
Aw. Sorry, kiddo.

184
00:08:29,885 --> 00:08:31,929
Your mom is no fun.

185
00:08:32,304 --> 00:08:33,847
Excuse me, I'm fun.

186
00:08:34,056 --> 00:08:35,057
So I can color my hair?

187
00:08:35,265 --> 00:08:36,308
Not a chance.

188
00:08:36,517 --> 00:08:37,851
But I'm very much fun.

189
00:08:38,936 --> 00:08:40,604
Whatever you need to believe.

190
00:08:40,813 --> 00:08:41,897
Mein fiihrer.

191
00:08:53,867 --> 00:08:54,493
Dad?

192
00:08:54,702 --> 00:08:55,702
Yeah?

193
00:08:55,911 --> 00:08:57,997
Would you like to have a conversation?

194
00:08:58,497 --> 00:09:00,332
Yeah. Sure. Absolutely.

195
00:09:00,541 --> 00:09:02,835
All right, what would you like to talk about?

196
00:09:04,044 --> 00:09:06,171
Um, well, let's see.

197
00:09:06,380 --> 00:09:10,216
Uh... have you given much thought to what you want to be when you grow up?

198
00:09:11,093 --> 00:09:12,177
I have.

199
00:09:12,553 --> 00:09:13,553
Great.

200
00:09:17,224 --> 00:09:18,726
And what would that be?

201
00:09:20,102 --> 00:09:21,895
Oh. Most likely a scientist.

202
00:09:22,104 --> 00:09:25,524
Unless I stay in Texas, then I'm thinking cattle baron.

203
00:09:25,733 --> 00:09:26,817
Cattle baron?

204
00:09:27,026 --> 00:09:29,111
Assuming I don't have to touch the cows.

205
00:09:29,778 --> 00:09:31,155
Goes without saying.

206
00:09:31,780 --> 00:09:33,907
Did you always want to be a football coach?

207
00:09:34,366 --> 00:09:35,659
Well, I always wanted to play.

208
00:09:35,868 --> 00:09:37,119
At least till I got hurt.

209
00:09:37,786 --> 00:09:38,786
Mm.

210
00:09:39,163 --> 00:09:40,414
Were you a good player?

211
00:09:40,622 --> 00:09:42,750
Eh, not really.

212
00:09:42,958 --> 00:09:44,626
I was just bigger than the other kids.

213
00:09:45,294 --> 00:09:48,589
So you compensated for mediocrity by being large.

214
00:09:50,257 --> 00:09:51,258
I guess.

215
00:09:51,884 --> 00:09:53,343
That works for cattle as well.

216
00:09:53,552 --> 00:09:55,137
Oh, well, thanks for pointing that out.

217
00:09:55,387 --> 00:09:56,387
You're welcome.

218
00:09:58,557 --> 00:10:00,434
You might want to open a window.

219
00:10:00,642 --> 00:10:02,019
Oh, boy.

220
00:10:05,230 --> 00:10:06,231
0h...

221
00:10:06,815 --> 00:10:09,318
J'j' whoa, oh, oh, yeah... j'j'

222
00:10:11,320 --> 00:10:13,238
my head is so hot.

223
00:10:13,447 --> 00:10:16,075
She is such a hoot.

224
00:10:18,077 --> 00:10:19,495
You okay? Fine.

225
00:10:21,121 --> 00:10:22,873
Okay, don't tell me.

226
00:10:23,665 --> 00:10:24,750
So hot...

227
00:10:26,043 --> 00:10:30,714
I don't like you making me out to be the bad guy just 'cause I won't let my daughter do whatever she wants.

228
00:10:30,923 --> 00:10:33,258
I gave you a lot of freedom, you turned out okay.

229
00:10:33,467 --> 00:10:34,760
You didn't give me freedom.

230
00:10:34,968 --> 00:10:36,261
You were never around.

231
00:10:36,553 --> 00:10:37,930
Is that so?

232
00:10:38,138 --> 00:10:42,009
I guarantee I made supper for charlene and Edward more times than you ever did.

233
00:10:42,184 --> 00:10:43,477
I basically raised 'em.

234
00:10:43,685 --> 00:10:45,020
You think I was out dancing?

235
00:10:45,229 --> 00:10:49,358
I was out working two jobs so your daddy could lose all our money on that damn chain of fotomats!

236
00:10:49,566 --> 00:10:53,237
It wasn't daddy's fault that those little things blew over every time there was a storm.

237
00:10:53,445 --> 00:10:54,445
Hmm.

238
00:10:55,322 --> 00:10:57,324
Seriously, I'm melting.

239
00:11:00,369 --> 00:11:01,036
Dead armadillo.

240
00:11:01,245 --> 00:11:02,454
That's three for me.

241
00:11:03,372 --> 00:11:05,457
This is a terrible driving game.

242
00:11:05,833 --> 00:11:07,376
Is it roadkill if it's still twitchin'?

243
00:11:08,585 --> 00:11:11,463
Huh, both alive and dead, just like schrodinger's cat.

244
00:11:12,005 --> 00:11:13,298
I didn't know he had a cat.

245
00:11:13,841 --> 00:11:14,961
You've heard of schrodinger?

246
00:11:15,259 --> 00:11:18,178
Sure. It's the kid from Charlie brown who plays the piano.

247
00:11:18,387 --> 00:11:19,930
Lucy's got a crush on him.

248
00:11:20,889 --> 00:11:23,600
Schrodinger's cat is a thought experiment.

249
00:11:23,976 --> 00:11:28,981
A cat in a box is exposed to poison, and is both alive and dead until it is observed.

250
00:11:29,189 --> 00:11:30,941
So the cat's name is schrodinger?

251
00:11:31,233 --> 00:11:32,233
No.

252
00:11:32,317 --> 00:11:33,527
Well, what's its name?

253
00:11:33,735 --> 00:11:35,237
Its name doesn't matter.

254
00:11:35,445 --> 00:11:36,905
It does if the cat was dead.

255
00:11:37,114 --> 00:11:39,116
Otherwise, what are you gonna put on his tombstone?

256
00:11:39,366 --> 00:11:41,243
Not likely the cat's getting a tombstone.

257
00:11:41,451 --> 00:11:42,995
It would in a pet cemetery.

258
00:11:44,454 --> 00:11:46,623
Fine, the cat's name is mittens.

259
00:11:46,832 --> 00:11:48,458
Because he has little white feet?

260
00:11:49,084 --> 00:11:50,085
Sure.

261
00:11:50,294 --> 00:11:54,423
So, in this thought experiment, do you think mittens is dead or alive?

262
00:11:54,631 --> 00:11:57,301
There's no way of saying until you open the box.

263
00:11:58,260 --> 00:11:59,469
Oh, come on.

264
00:12:00,262 --> 00:12:02,764
Optimistically, I would choose to believe he's alive.

265
00:12:03,015 --> 00:12:04,725
Yes! Oh, thank goodness.

266
00:12:05,100 --> 00:12:06,435
Oh, dead crow.

267
00:12:06,727 --> 00:12:08,478
There ain't no doubt about that one.

268
00:12:15,152 --> 00:12:17,070
The toilet was sanitized for my protection.

269
00:12:17,279 --> 00:12:18,822
I love this place.

270
00:12:19,656 --> 00:12:21,325
Dad, can we go to reptile world?

271
00:12:21,533 --> 00:12:24,912
No. They got a snake so big it can eat a whole chicken.

272
00:12:25,120 --> 00:12:27,164
Oh, well, in that case, no.

273
00:12:27,497 --> 00:12:29,082
Aw. Let's get some sleep.

274
00:12:29,374 --> 00:12:32,377
We got to get up early if we're gonna get to cape canaveral in time for liftoff.

275
00:12:32,586 --> 00:12:34,296
I'm so excited, I don't know if I can.

276
00:12:34,504 --> 00:12:36,506
Well, buddy, you're gonna have to try, all right?

277
00:12:36,715 --> 00:12:39,009
You two share that bed, I'll take this one.

278
00:12:39,218 --> 00:12:40,594
-Nuh-uh.

279
00:12:41,511 --> 00:12:43,096
Come on, fellas, I'm the biggest.

280
00:12:43,305 --> 00:12:45,015
It makes sense that I get a bed to myself.

281
00:12:46,475 --> 00:12:47,768
-Nuh-uh.

282
00:12:51,146 --> 00:12:53,315
We'll flip for it. Georgie, call it.

283
00:12:53,523 --> 00:12:54,858
Heads.

284
00:12:56,109 --> 00:12:57,486
Not your day.

285
00:12:57,778 --> 00:12:58,779
Dang it.

286
00:12:59,363 --> 00:13:01,365
That looked like heads. Go brush your teeth.

287
00:13:05,327 --> 00:13:06,620
This really works?

288
00:13:06,828 --> 00:13:11,583
Your hair will look just as pretty tomorrow.

289
00:13:11,959 --> 00:13:13,377
Now, come on, let's tuck you in.

290
00:13:14,962 --> 00:13:16,964
I'm glad I don't have orange hair.

291
00:13:17,172 --> 00:13:18,423
Me, too, baby.

292
00:13:18,632 --> 00:13:20,300
I want to be more like Madonna.

293
00:13:20,884 --> 00:13:21,969
Are you trying to kill me?

294
00:13:22,177 --> 00:13:23,303
'Cause if you are, good job.

295
00:13:28,308 --> 00:13:30,227
Why is she only like a virgin?

296
00:13:30,435 --> 00:13:31,795
Good night!

297
00:13:34,982 --> 00:13:36,858
You ready to finish our conversation?

298
00:13:37,067 --> 00:13:38,107
There's nothing to finish.

299
00:13:38,277 --> 00:13:40,153
I raised myself like a jungle child.

300
00:13:40,362 --> 00:13:41,362
End of story.

301
00:13:41,446 --> 00:13:43,615
Oh, stop being so dramatic.

302
00:13:43,824 --> 00:13:47,411
You think I didn't feel bad not being around more than I wanted to be?

303
00:13:47,995 --> 00:13:48,995
Did you?

304
00:13:49,955 --> 00:13:51,123
A little bit.

305
00:13:52,291 --> 00:13:54,001
I'm teasing, come on. Of course I did.

306
00:13:54,209 --> 00:13:57,045
Why else would I have begged you and George to move back to medford?

307
00:13:57,254 --> 00:13:58,814
So you could be with your grandchildren.

308
00:13:58,964 --> 00:13:59,964
And you.

309
00:14:00,465 --> 00:14:01,591
Really? Yeah.

310
00:14:01,800 --> 00:14:03,945
You're the only one of my children still talking to me.

311
00:14:03,969 --> 00:14:05,095
No surprise there.

312
00:14:05,512 --> 00:14:08,140
Besides, you raised yourself better than I ever could.

313
00:14:08,765 --> 00:14:10,267
You actually believe that?

314
00:14:10,726 --> 00:14:13,979
No, but it would help my cause if you did.

315
00:14:22,904 --> 00:14:23,904
Your hair looks pretty.

316
00:14:24,072 --> 00:14:25,407
Enough.

317
00:14:35,167 --> 00:14:36,167
' Dad? '

318
00:14:38,086 --> 00:14:39,086
dad?

319
00:14:40,714 --> 00:14:41,714
Dad?

320
00:14:42,341 --> 00:14:43,884
Dad.

321
00:14:44,343 --> 00:14:44,968
What?

322
00:14:45,177 --> 00:14:46,636
Georgie keeps kicking me.

323
00:14:47,346 --> 00:14:48,346
Kick him back.

324
00:14:48,472 --> 00:14:50,474
I'd rather not touch him.

325
00:14:53,560 --> 00:14:54,644
You want to sleep with me?

326
00:14:54,853 --> 00:14:56,313
Yes, thank you.

327
00:14:59,983 --> 00:15:01,109
Yeah.

328
00:15:03,612 --> 00:15:04,821
Got enough room?

329
00:15:05,781 --> 00:15:07,074
Yes.

330
00:15:11,787 --> 00:15:13,705
You throw off a lot of heat.

331
00:15:14,998 --> 00:15:15,999
Sorry.

332
00:15:17,084 --> 00:15:19,795
That's all right. It's kind of nice.

333
00:15:31,640 --> 00:15:33,767
Do they launch those shuttles in the rain?

334
00:15:34,559 --> 00:15:36,520
I think a light rain's okay.

335
00:15:40,357 --> 00:15:41,650
Oh, no.

336
00:15:41,858 --> 00:15:42,858
It'll pass.

337
00:15:43,902 --> 00:15:45,404
Just get some sleep.

338
00:15:52,369 --> 00:15:54,121
It didn't pass.

339
00:15:54,913 --> 00:15:56,164
Sheldon, I'm real sorry.

340
00:16:04,840 --> 00:16:05,966
Can I tell you a secret?

341
00:16:07,217 --> 00:16:09,428
I never understood how lightning works.

342
00:16:09,845 --> 00:16:11,930
Didn't they teach you that in high school?

343
00:16:12,139 --> 00:16:16,268
They probably did, but I got hit in the head a lot playing football.

344
00:16:17,936 --> 00:16:19,104
Would you explain it to me?

345
00:16:20,147 --> 00:16:25,318
Well, when positive and negative charges grow large enough, a giant spark occurs in the cloud.

346
00:16:25,527 --> 00:16:28,989
Ah, that-that's pretty cool. What causes the thunder?

347
00:16:29,197 --> 00:16:32,993
It's a shock wave from particles heated to 10,000 degrees.

348
00:16:33,702 --> 00:16:34,702
Interesting.

349
00:16:34,870 --> 00:16:37,122
You want to know what's really interesting? Hmm?

350
00:16:37,330 --> 00:16:41,376
Aristotle thought that the sound of thunder was due to a collision between two clouds.

351
00:16:41,585 --> 00:16:45,380
He believed the clouds were expelling air, in the way a log on a fire crackles...

352
00:16:45,589 --> 00:16:53,889
I didn't realize until years later that my father was only asking questions about lightning and thunder to cheer me up.

353
00:16:54,097 --> 00:16:58,101
In fact, he would often pretend to be dumb just to make me feel better.

354
00:16:58,602 --> 00:17:00,061
Looks like rain.

355
00:17:00,270 --> 00:17:03,231
My brother, on the other hand, didn't have to pretend.

356
00:17:11,573 --> 00:17:13,909
Okay, on the count of three, we run to the car.

357
00:17:14,117 --> 00:17:16,453
Ready? One, two... Wait.

358
00:17:16,661 --> 00:17:18,079
I want shotgun going back.

359
00:17:18,622 --> 00:17:20,957
Fine, you get shotgun. Okay, here we go.

360
00:17:21,166 --> 00:17:25,045
One, two... I still think we should wait till the rain slows down.

361
00:17:25,253 --> 00:17:26,613
George sr.: No, we got to get home.

362
00:17:26,796 --> 00:17:28,507
I got work tomorrow, you guys got school.

363
00:17:28,715 --> 00:17:30,133
You do realize I'll get wet?

364
00:17:30,342 --> 00:17:31,885
It's just water, Sheldon.

365
00:17:32,135 --> 00:17:34,387
All right. Just making sure you realize.

366
00:17:35,263 --> 00:17:36,556
All right, here we go. Ready?

367
00:17:36,765 --> 00:17:38,934
One, two, three.

368
00:17:57,327 --> 00:17:59,204
Buddy, I thought we had a plan.

369
00:17:59,538 --> 00:18:00,830
You had a plan.

370
00:18:11,091 --> 00:18:12,926
N n

371
00:18:17,722 --> 00:18:23,311
adult Sheldon: I never did get to see a launch in person, but that was the best trip I ever had.

372
00:18:28,316 --> 00:18:31,861
I wish I had told my father while he was alive.
